ew & Scrutiny Committee","meeting_id":5948,"meeting_date":"2026-06-09","published":"2026-05-28","filename":"mg25-central-bedfordshire-2026-06-09-corporate-resources-overvi-83204-appendix-c-revenue-treasury-management-d.pdf"},{"id":83334,"title":"Appendix C \u2013 Revenue Treasury Management Dashboard","url":"https://centralbeds.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s83334/appendix-c-revenue-treasury-management-dashboard.pdf","type":"other","type_label":"Paper","weight":1,"committee":"Social Care, Health & Housing Overview & Scrutiny Committee","meeting_id":5984,"meeting_date":"2026-06-15","published":"2026-06-05","filename":"mg25-central-bedfordshire-2026-06-15-social-care-health-housing-83334-appendix-c-revenue-treasury-management-d.pdf"},{"id":83443,"title":"DSG contingency budgets update Jun 26","url":"https://centralbeds.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s83443/dsg-contingency-budgets-update-jun-26.pdf","type":"other","type_label":"Paper","weight":1,"committee":"Schools Forum","meeting_id":6047,"meeting_date":"2026-06-22","published":"2026-06-15","filename":"mg25-central-bedfordshire-2026-06-22-schools-forum-83443-dsg-contingency-budgets-update-jun-26.pdf"},{"id":83837,"title":"Saxon Pool and Leisure Centre improvements","url":"https://centralbeds.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s83837/saxon-pool-and-leisure-centre-improvements.pdf","type":"other","type_label":"Paper","weight":1,"committee":"Executive","meeting_id":5955,"meeting_date":"2026-08-04","published":"2026-07-23","filename":"mg25-central-bedfordshire-2026-08-04-executive-83837-saxon-pool-and-leisure-centre-improvemen.pdf"}],"notes":{"id":"mg25","gss":"mg25","schema":2,"council":"Central Bedfordshire","paper":{"title":"Appendix B - Revenue Debt Management","committee":"Social Care, Health & Housing Overview & Scrutiny Committee","meeting_date":"2026-06-15","doc_id":83333,"url":"https://centralbeds.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s83333/appendix-b-revenue-debt-management.pdf","pdf_local":"/Users/philipsmith/Documents/PWLBtoday Council Papers/mg25-central-bedfordshire-2026-06-15-social-care-health-housing-83333-appendix-b-revenue-debt-management.pdf","pages":1,"text":"papers/mg25/83333.txt","financial_year":"2025-26","note":"One page. This is a receivables/write-offs paper \u2014 'debt' throughout means money owed TO the council by service users, tenants and other customers (sundry debtors). It is NOT the council's treasury/borrowing debt. No CFR, no PWLB, no external borrowing, no LOBOs, no MRP, no loan maturity profile, no interest rates, no prudential indicators. The paper is a standing arrears-management item at the Social Care, Health & Housing O&S committee (roughly two-thirds of the \u00a333.6m arrears book sits with Adult Social Care & Housing, and the aging matches the residential-care-fees-recovered-from-estates pattern). No companion treasury papers were listed in the brief and none is referenced by the appendix itself."},"facts":[{"key":"receivables_total","value":"\u00a333.6m sundry debtors outstanding at March 2026. Split: \u00a316.2m under 60 days (48%), \u00a317.4m over 61 days (52%). Grand total in the aged-debt table foots to \u00a333,593k, ties to the \u00a333.6m figure in paragraph 1.","as_at":"2026-03-31","source":{"page":1,"table":"Paragraph 1 + Aged Debt Table","text":"papers/mg25/83333.txt"},"note":"NOT treasury debt. This is receivables \u2014 money owed TO Central Bedfordshire by service users, tenants and other customers. Recorded here so the note is complete about what the paper actually said, not because it is a PWLB-side figure."},{"key":"receivables_over_60d_composition","value":"Of the \u00a317.4m over 61 days: \u00a314.1m actively being chased, \u00a30.7m on instalment arrangements, \u00a32.4m through legal channels, \u00a30.07m secured with charges, \u00a30.1m in dispute, \u00a30.06m identified for write-off. A further \u00a32.1m relates to house sales.","as_at":"2026-03-31","source":{"page":1,"table":"Paragraph 2","text":"papers/mg25/83333.txt"},"note":"The \u00a32.1m 'house sales' line is consistent with the well-known adult social care fee pattern \u2014 residential care charges accrued against clients' estates and recovered when a property is sold."},{"key":"receivables_by_directorate","value":"Adult Social Care & Housing carries \u00a322.977m of the \u00a333.593m total (68.4%), of which \u00a310.340m (45% of the ASC line) sits in the '1 year and over' bucket. Place & Communities \u00a36.188m, Resources & Organisational Change \u00a31.855m, Public Health \u00a31.564m, Children & Families \u00a30.503m, Finance \u00a30.282m, Monitoring Officer \u00a30.159m, HRA \u00a30.095m, Schools \u00a30.056m, Unallocated \u00a3-0.086m. Chief Executive nil.","as_at":"2026-03-31","source":{"page":1,"table":"Aged Debt Table by Directorate","text":"papers/mg25/83333.txt"},"note":"Public Health and Schools rows print '0%' across every aging bucket despite non-zero amounts \u2014 a spreadsheet formatting artefact in the source (the amounts are correct; the percentages did not populate against the total). Do not read significance into the 0% cells."},{"key":"write_offs_2025_26","value":"245 write-offs totalling \u00a3415,948.68 in 2025/26. Band split: 230 at <\u00a35k = \u00a3130,788.92; 8 at \u00a35k-\u00a310k = \u00a349,415.92; 5 at \u00a310k-\u00a350k = \u00a398,420.68; 2 at >\u00a350k = \u00a3137,323.16.","as_at":"2026-03-31","source":{"page":1,"table":"Write Off Summary \u2014 Annual Summary","text":"papers/mg25/83333.txt"},"note":"The two >\u00a350k write-offs alone account for a third of the annual write-off value. Amounts and count reconcile to the printed total to the penny."}],"reconciliation":{"written":"2026-08-15","loan_book_tie":"Not applicable to this paper \u2014 the appendix carries no treasury figures. Recorded for completeness only, so a future treasury paper from this council can cite the position without re-running: `python3 monitor/outreach/price_book.py --find 'Central Bedfordshire'` returns 'CENTRAL BEDFORDSHIRE COUNCIL' (exact name). At 2026-03-31 our price book holds 31 PWLB loans totalling \u00a3336,774,618 at a weighted 2.9792%, mix 31 MATURITY (no EIP/annuity). At today's date (2026-08-15) 28 loans remain live totalling \u00a3281.42m. NONE of this is claimed against the paper \u2014 there is no printed treasury table in this appendix to reconcile against.","balance_sheet_identity":"Not applicable. The identity CFR \u2212 external borrowing \u2212 other long-term liabilities = internal borrowing requires all three inputs; none appears in this receivables appendix.","budget_tie":"Not applicable \u2014 this is not a budget monitoring paper. The \u00a333.593m grand-total row of the aged-debt table foots correctly to the \u00a333.6m figure quoted in paragraph 1. The 245 write-offs sum to \u00a3415,948.68 exactly (230 + 8 + 5 + 2 = 245; \u00a3130,788.92 + \u00a349,415.92 + \u00a398,420.68 + \u00a3137,323.16 = \u00a3415,948.68 to the penny).","rates_check":"Not applicable \u2014 the paper prints no interest rates. For reference only, the prevailing PWLB curve on 14 August 2026 (notice 314/26 PM) put the council's 28 live PWLB loans at an indicative net discount of \u00a399.05m (35.2% of principal), 24 loans below par and 4 above. This is not a claim against the paper \u2014 it comes from our own price book against the current DMO curve."},"meetings":{},"summary":{"written":"2026-08-15","text":"<p>Central Bedfordshire's <b>Appendix B \u2014 Revenue Debt Management</b> to the Social Care, Health &amp; Housing O&amp;S committee on 15 June 2026 is a receivables aging and bad-debt write-off paper. The word 'debt' throughout means money owed TO the council by service users, tenants and other customers \u2014 not the council's own borrowing. The whole document is one page: an aged-debt table split by directorate, a short narrative on how the over-60-days book is being pursued, and an annual write-off summary.</p><p>Headline: \u00a333.6m of sundry debtors at 31 March 2026, of which \u00a316.2m (48%) sits within 60 days and \u00a317.4m (52%) is over 61 days. Adult Social Care &amp; Housing carries \u00a322.977m of the total (68.4%), and \u00a310.340m of the ASC line sits in the '1 year and over' bucket \u2014 the well-known residential-care-fees-recovered-from-estates pattern (paragraph 2's \u00a32.1m 'in respect of house sales' is consistent). Annual write-offs for 2025/26 totalled \u00a3415,948.68 across 245 cases, with two individual cases &gt;\u00a350k accounting for \u00a3137k of the total. All internal footings tie to the penny.</p><p>The paper contains <b>no treasury content whatsoever</b>: no CFR, no external borrowing, no PWLB, no LOBOs, no maturity profile, no interest rates, no MRP, no prudential indicators. There is nothing to reconcile against our PWLB loan book (though for completeness we hold 31 PWLB loans / \u00a3336.77m / weighted 2.9792% at 2026-03-31 for the correctly-named borrower 'CENTRAL BEDFORDSHIRE COUNCIL'). The balance-sheet identity is not applicable because none of its inputs is stated. The committee is scrutiny and the audience is Adult Social Care members, not the S151.</p><p>Per PIPELINE.md, this is the 'revenue outturn / planning briefing / schools funding monitor' case: a paper with no treasury content is a thin note by definition and no email is drafted. Central Bedfordshire remains a viable outreach target \u2014 the council has a live PWLB book and publishes a Treasury Management Strategy and outturn report elsewhere in the calendar \u2014 but not off this appendix. Revisit when a Treasury Management Strategy, Mid-Year Review or Annual Outturn Report comes through in the mg25 slot.</p>"},"contacts":[],"status":{"state":"read-thin","written_up":true,"contact":false,"as_at":"2026-08-15","source_text_held":true,"note":"Read in full: the paper is a single-page revenue-debt-management appendix to a Social Care O&S outturn cover report. Zero treasury content \u2014 this is receivables aging and write-offs, not the council's own borrowing. No companion treasury papers were listed in the brief and the appendix references none. PWLB loan book reconciliation was run for completeness (31 loans, \u00a3336.77m, 2.9792% at 2026-03-31) but there is nothing in the paper to reconcile it against. Balance-sheet identity not applicable \u2014 none of CFR / external borrowing / OLTL is stated. Per PIPELINE.md 'only when a paper carries no treasury content whatsoever \u2014 a revenue outturn, a planning briefing, a schools funding monitor \u2014 write the note recording exactly that and draft nothing.' No officer contact recorded because the paper's audience is Adult Social Care O&S members, not the S151, and the appendix carries no author byline or officer address. Revisit when a Treasury Management Strategy, Mid-Year Review or Annual Outturn Report from Central Bedfordshire comes through the queue \u2014 the council has a live 31-loan PWLB book that would give a real hook against the right paper.","state_was":"read-thin-no-email"},"emails":{"officer":null}}}